WEBVTT

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:03.540
<i>Shunsuke has overcome
his troubles with his teammates</i>

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.040
<i>and just when I've started to think that
the distance between us has lessened,</i>

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.940
<i>now we're being tangled
up with an underclass boy.</i>

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.350
<i>I have a bad feeling about
more trouble incoming...</i>

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.830
And so he keeps doing nothing
but make terrible jokes.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.800
Oh, Ryo-chan, good morning.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.390
I told you I don't want stuff like this!

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.130
Oh, it's so cute.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.770
Isn't it though? I thought
it would match him perfectly!

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.520
Ryo-chan, you're just too cute for words!

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.130
I'm totally taking a picture.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.610
Even though we have three girls,
that kind of thing suits you the best.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.880
Stop it!

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.370
I hate this kind of junk!

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.080
And stop just going into my
room whenever you want.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.060
I won't forgive you if it happens again!

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:10.290
Our little sugar is just so cute.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.340
Don't call me "sugar!"

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:17.510
<b>Factoid: The name "sugar" is a nickname
 Westerners use as a term of endearment.</b>

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.580
That just makes him cuter.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.900
Broken Rose-Colored Clouds

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.860
Hey, that boy is really cute, don't you think?

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.610
Oh, totally! I want to dress him up as a girl!

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.010
Oh, that Purin clear file is super cute!

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.410
Right?

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:09.640
Is it new?

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.520
Was there one for Melody-chan?

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.330
I believe there was.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.750
I got it at the Yokohama Sanrio store though.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:18.500
What?

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.480
You finally managed to go there by yourself.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.520
Daddy is so proud of you!

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.900
Thanks to your help.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.890
Shunsuke, if I find one for
Kitty-san, do you want it?

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.130
Of course I do.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.210
What a shame.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.160
They're so cool but their
interests are kind of weird.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.400
Not manly at all.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.430
Seriously.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.040
What is it?

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.620
Aren't you ashamed of yourselves?

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:55.710
Huh?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.050
Umm... about what?

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.090
Because!

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.560
You're a bunch of guys sitting
around chattering like girls,

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.010
that's why I asked if you're ashamed!

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.860
It's weird to have girly
interests in high school!

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.370
You know,

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.730
I could smile and overlook this
if you were just talking about me,

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:23.240
but you're saying this about Kouta
and Shunsuke, too, aren't you?

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.470
Hey!

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.660
If that's the case...

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.990
I won't just ignore it!

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.510
Yuu, knock it off.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.280
What's so wrong about high
school students liking Sanrio?

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.040
Even if you try to threaten me,
a weirdo is still a weirdo!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.930
So that means you're asking
for a fight then, right?

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:41.630
Wait!

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:49.810
I don't know what's happened,
but you shouldn't resort to violence.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:51.830
Calm down.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.570
You're right.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.190
I just got a little too worked up.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.670
Um, you're an underclassman, right?

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.080
Sorry for scaring you like that.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.620
Shut up, weirdo!

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.160
Hey!

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.210
I hate them!

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.560
You're putting too much strength
in your shoulder like that

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.110
and you're gripping the bow too much.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:37.940
Yes sir!

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.760
You're both captain and a starter,

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:50.410
you should focus on practice and leave it to
 the second-years to guide the underclassmen.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:54.040
I'm not going to call on others
when I was asked to help.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.620
You're so serious.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:03.380
<b>Prefectural Hijirikawa High School Archery Club</b>

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:01.310
You haven't gotten to practice much since
the student council takes up your time, right?

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:05.780
Being the student council president and captain
of the archery club are positions that I wanted.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.340
<b>Shooting Practice</b>

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.720
I can't neglect either of them.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.850
I guess that's true.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:14.890
Nishimiya!

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.060
Nishimiya Ryo!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:23.110
I heard about what happened yesterday
from Mizuno and the others.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:24.860
You going to lecture me?

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:26.870
I want to ask you something.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.740
Morning practice is over,
so could you wait a bit for me there?

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.370
I'm counting on you.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.300
Wh-Why am I actually waiting like he asked?

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:55.950
Nishimiya.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.980
You're from yesterday,

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.540
Yoshino Shunsuke from class 2-4.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.490
You know your stuff.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.950
Because I'm the student council president.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:23.540
I saw Nishimiya a short time ago but I
wasn't able to talk to him.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.220
I figured I'd try to talk to him later.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.920
Please don't trouble yourself over it.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.680
No, I make sure things are
resolved when I'm involved.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.430
You're a really meddlesome person, aren't you?

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.680
I'm told that a lot.

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:46.410
I'm not angry. I know there are guys
who hate it when other guys talk like that.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:47.690
I don't think like that.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.650
Making a ruckus in the
library isn't a good thing,

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.280
but it doesn't matter what others
say about your interests, right?

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:58.120
You're pretty flexible.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.210
That's one I don't hear often.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.950
Hey, Yoshino!

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.650
I'm coming!

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.860
Please excuse me.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:06.660
Sure.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.450
Really though, don't trouble yourself.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:13.430
I'm sure they're not angry anymore either.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.590
What the heck is with that guy?!

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:20.140
Even though he totally has a face
more suited for Sanrio goods than us!

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.470
You really hold grudges.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.880
I can't forgive anyone who
speaks badly about my friends.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.840
Speaking of, why aren't you both angry about this?

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.700
It doesn't matter.

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:39.490
I don't really have much confidence,

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:44.330
so when he said that stuff,
I kind of thought he was right.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:47.630
Don't take anything he said seriously.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:52.760
Everyone has different interests and
no one else has any right to comment.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:55.510
The student council president
said about the same thing.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.350
Oh, the president did?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.830
Nice, I want be friends with him.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:00.930
With the president?

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:03.430
He might come in pretty handy.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.290
I don't think he's that kind of person.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:10.180
True, he seems pretty stiff.

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:12.650
Well, I'm sure he would to you.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.900
Kouta, you've got some nerve,

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:17.410
you cheeky jerk!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.000
Stop it, I'll spill it!

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:25.460
He seems to be trying to settle things between
us and that first-year from yesterday.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.650
Hey, stop! I'm going to spill!

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:27.840
Is that right?

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:34.300
I feel kind of bad about that.
I guess I went a little too far.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.550
Yuu, you're such a nice guy deep down.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.610
Oh, I can have it?

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.410
Yep.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.810
I'll give you mine too,
so just be in a better mood.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.150
Lucky me!

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:49.320
Excuse me, could you please
get Nishimiya Ryo for me?

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.560
S-Sure.

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:52.570
Hey! Is Nishimiya here?

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.220
He doesn't seem to be here right now.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.820
I see, thanks anyway.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.420
You're pretty cheap if all you need
is some fried chicken to make you feel better.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.890
From now on we'll just give you fried
chicken when anything happens.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:09.830
That's not why.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.300
I just realized that I can't
hold on to a grudge forever.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:15.690
Because of the fried chicken, right?

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.720
I won't say that that's not it, too,

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:20.720
but I'm an adult.

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.130
Perfect timing!

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:28.140
Yuu, don't!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:31.260
I'm not! I'm just going to
show him my mature side!

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.280
You dropped this.

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:43.730
Don't be on guard like that,
I'm not mad anymore.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.040
That looks heavy, I'll help you.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:51.080
I don't want any help from a weirdo!

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.790
<i>Help from a weirdo...
From a weirdo... weirdo...</i>

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:04.220
What the heck is his deal?!

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.900
And we're back to this.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.650
Should we go eat fried chicken again?

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:13.230
He really seems to hate us though.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:18.480
Maybe it's more that he hates
himself rather than us?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.820
Why do you think that?

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:25.650
I just know that until
recently I felt like that.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.240
Like something was really
irritating me deep down.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:37.960
I'm so weak.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:39.400
So frustrating.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.630
Did you hear all that?

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.970
Please don't say anything
about it to anyone else.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:02.880
And they're totally selling it in Shibuya.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:03.740
Really?

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.700
I'm going to get it right away.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.640
I get paid by my job today
so I'll head there asap.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:09.700
Hey!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.830
Wasn't that girl pretty cute?

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.630
Stupid, he was wearing a boys' uniform.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.880
Seriously?

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.320
You really don't see anything
but the face, do you?

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:22.470
You three there, wait!

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.470
Ah, President?

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:30.150
It's rude to bump into someone and then
keep going without saying anything!

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:33.480
You should apologize properly
when you trouble someone!

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.140
Oh, y-you're right.

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.090
I'm sorry!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.880
Thank you.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.000
I just did the right thing.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:49.010
You should also do the right
thing and apologize

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:52.250
for blowing up at Mizuno and
the others in the library yesterday.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.240
Why didn't you wait for me this morning?

00:12:56.950 --> 00:13:00.050
I'm not going to wait just cause you ask me to.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.490
That's just an excuse.

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:05.300
If you didn't want to wait, you
should've just told me then and there.

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:10.010
I can't refuse an upperclassman
when they speak to me like that.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.910
Then in that case, don't you think

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:17.590
it's even more rude to an upperclassman
to just leave without saying anything?

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:19.480
That's...

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:21.640
That's?

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.490
I'm sorry about that.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.490
Okay then, that's good.

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:36.410
You should apologize when you're in the wrong.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.410
I'll get to the point then.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:45.490
Why did you blow up at Mizuno
and the others in the library yesterday?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:50.570
I heard from them that you got in
a fight with them over their interests,

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:52.620
but will you tell me your side of the story?

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.720
There's no need to.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.190
I'll just go apologize to them later.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.410
No, that's not enough.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.730
While that might resolve things
for Mizuno and the others,

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.530
it won't resolve things for you.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.860
Whether it resolves things for
me has nothing to do with you.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.320
It does!

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.700
You are a student here

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.650
and I am the student council president
who represents the students.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:19.410
There isn't a student problem
that has nothing to do with me.

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:21.500
You're way too serious.

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:24.190
I'm often told that's my disposition.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:27.570
There might be something I can help with.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.380
Won't you talk to me?

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:34.100
Please meddle in the lives of those
closer to you rather than mine.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.310
Don't avoid this!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:42.260
People will only be honest with
you when you're honest with them.

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.070
I want to help you.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:51.070
Will you talk to me?

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.070
Or won't you?

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:07.420
Ever since I was little, I've often been
treated like a girl because of how I look.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:11.590
Ah... from a distance I can see
how people would think you're a girl.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.470
I really hate that.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.490
Oh, okay then. I'm sorry.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.760
But, everyone around me
just wouldn't understand

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:28.270
and they'd continue to force girlish
things on me, even though I'm a boy.

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:32.320
After all that, I think I got
irritated because I was watching

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:36.790
guys who were more manly than
me talking like a bunch of girls.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:41.610
You keep saying things like "everyone
around me" and "because they were talking"

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:43.040
and blaming others.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:44.530
Huh?

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.250
Nishimiya Ryo,

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:50.260
you have to face yourself properly.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:52.540
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.090
Is it from some moral textbook or something?

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:55.780
I told you not to avoid this!

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.750
You have to face yourself properly.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.030
You're probably right.

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.030
Okay!

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:16.980
Then, I'll go with you tomorrow so you
can apologize to Mizuno and the others.

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:19.620
Got it.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:23.950
That's right, feel free to consult me
should anything come up again.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:25.080
My cell number is...

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:26.830
Phones are a pain.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:28.590
Okay then.

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.700
Line is easier.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.090
I'm home.

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:41.720
Ryo-chan, look, look!

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:43.810
We found some old pictures.

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.560
Come here, look!

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:52.370
Ryo-chan, you used to love Little
Twin Stars when you were little.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:55.240
Speaking of, you haven't collected
anything with it lately, have you?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.450
That's because I'm a high schooler now.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:00.870
Aww, but it would be cute even now!
It would totally suit you.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.870
I don't want to be thought of as cute.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.920
That side of you just makes you cuter.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.760
Let me hold you, sweetie!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:10.820
Huh?

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:19.830
I guess facing myself properly
means I have to face that, too?

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:28.770
<b>How are you feeling?</b>

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:27.560
How am I feeling?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.770
Nothing has changed from earlier.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:42.040
<b>I guess that makes sense.</b>

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:42.040
"I guess that makes sense."

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:48.500
Senpai, you haven't used
Line very much, have you?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.010
<b>Honestly, not mich.</b>

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.010
"Honestly, not mich."

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.510
<b>mich.</b>

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:55.510
"mich."

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:00.510
<b>Student Council Room</b>

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.260
It ended up as "mich".

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:05.480
Now then, time to work.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:12.660
Hey, working overtime again?

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.530
The student council are slave drivers.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:17.310
Don't say such bad things about people.

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:19.200
What do you need?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.530
Our team has been practicing
pretty passionately lately

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.270
and our consumable goods expenses are intense.

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:27.530
So you want us to increase
the soccer team's budget?

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.250
The team has improved considerably

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.670
and we might end this year on a good note.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.210
That will be a good thing
for stimulating club activities.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:37.720
I'll bring it up in the next council meeting.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.600
Thank you.

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:46.430
Anyway, aren't you taking on
too much of the work yourself?

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.090
Why don't you try passing it
off to other members?

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:50.460
It's in my nature.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:53.540
Once I take on something, I want
to see it through to the end.

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:55.440
You're going to pass out.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.190
I'll be fine.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:01.320
<b>Student Handbook</b>

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:01.320
I have the best recovery medicine available.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.180
The student handbook?

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:06.520
This is the key to all that.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.290
Sounds like a fantasy.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.540
It's more like

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.540
a fairy tale than a fantasy.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.020
<i>Huh? Huh?</i>

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:26.430
Sanrio Puroland Annual Passport

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:01.910
Captain, you're doing great today.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:03.930
All of them are aimed from the heart.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.050
That's because I refreshed myself.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:25.160
My student handbook?

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:29.780
Senpai's?

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:32.980
He's pretty careless.

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:09.580
And then—

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:10.440
Mornin'.

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:11.300
Morning.

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:12.580
Good job at practice.

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:13.930
Oh, President.

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.770
<b>Archery Hall</b>

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:15.810
Good morning!

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:17.180
Good morning.

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:19.480
Morning, just who I wanted to see.

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:22.720
About what happened the other day,
I talked to Nishimiya.

00:22:23.050 --> 00:22:26.290
I'm going to go with him to apologize to
you guys later, will you accept his apology?

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:28.910
Huh?! He said he would apologize?

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:30.030
Yeah.

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:33.010
Wow, you're amazing, President.

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:34.890
It's a difference in virtues I guess.

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:37.730
Are you trying to say that I don't
have any virtues, Shushu?!

00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:38.990
That's what I'm saying.

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:41.610
You jerk!

00:22:41.610 --> 00:22:43.000
Let go, come on.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:44.440
Hey, knock it off.

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:46.940
Do you feel that way too, Kouta?!

00:22:46.940 --> 00:22:48.720
Ow, ow, ow!

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:48.970
You really get along well.

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:50.720
That's right,

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:52.940
we do get along.

00:22:52.940 --> 00:22:54.740
We share the same interests, too.

00:22:55.110 --> 00:22:57.760
That's right, you did mention that.

00:22:57.760 --> 00:23:00.980
Other people don't really
some to understand us,

00:23:01.870 --> 00:23:03.480
even though she's super cute!

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:05.480
My Melody huh?

00:23:07.100 --> 00:23:08.650
You're really knowledgeable.

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:10.780
Yeah, the truth is I also—

00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:13.080
Nishimiya?

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:17.830
Huh.

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:20.180
That's a year pass to Puroland.

00:23:20.180 --> 00:23:21.110
Year pass?

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:22.950
An annual passport.

00:23:22.950 --> 00:23:27.000
You covered for them because
you're just like them, didn't you?!

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:31.110
You pretended to be worried about me,
but you were just protecting yourself!

00:23:32.270 --> 00:23:33.350
Nishimiya!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:40.410
Next Episode

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:39.410
Next time, "Above the Distant Clouds".
